{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleSumRule"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.saddle_cubic_of_ohtsuki_system","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.saddle_cubic_of_ohtsuki_system","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint.lean#L143-L153","doc":"**End to end**: a solution of Ohtsuki's critical-point system hands you a\nroot of the corpus's saddle cubic, namely `1 − x`.\n\nThis is the bridge from Ohtsuki's volume-conjecture saddle to the data\n`SaddleRoots` bundles — with the caveat, stated in the module header and gated as\nG4 of Route 71, that *which* root is the geometric one is analytic input that no\nalgebraic statement here supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.ohtsuki_cubic_iff_sq_eq_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.ohtsuki_cubic_iff_sq_eq_cube","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint.lean#L137-L141","doc":"The same, phrased in the `y² = (1−y)³` form the corpus carries: setting\n`y = 1 − x`, Ohtsuki's equation is the corpus's branch equation verbatim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.ohtsuki_cubic_iff_saddle_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.ohtsuki_cubic_iff_saddle_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint.lean#L125-L135","doc":"**THE IDENTIFICATION.**  `x` is an Ohtsuki critical point iff `1 − x` is a\nroot of the corpus's 5₂ saddle cubic.\n\n`FiveTwoSaddleSumRule.cubic_iff_sq_eq_cube` already gives\n`y³ − 2y² + 3y − 1 = 0 ↔ y² = (1−y)³`, so this says the two branch equations —\nOhtsuki's `x³ = (1−x)²` and the corpus's `y² = (1−y)³` — are the same equation\nin coordinates differing by `z ↦ 1 − z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.ohtsuki_cubic_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.ohtsuki_cubic_iff","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint.lean#L120-L123","doc":"`x³ = (1−x)²` in expanded form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.saddle_poly_of_ohtsuki_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.saddle_poly_of_ohtsuki_poly","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint.lean#L112-L118","doc":"**The two cubics are negatives of each other under `x = 1 − y`.**\n\n`(1−x)³ − 2(1−x)² + 3(1−x) − 1 = −(x³ − x² + 2x − 1)`.  One `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.one_sub_mul_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.one_sub_mul_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint.lean#L104-L108","doc":"The step the elimination turns on: `(1−x)(y−1) = x` is exactly `(1−x)y = 1`\nrearranged.  Recorded separately because it is the whole content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.ohtsuki_elim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.Ohtsuki.ohtsuki_elim","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoOhtsukiCriticalPoint.lean#L90-L102","doc":"**Ohtsuki's critical-point system eliminates to `x³ = (1−x)²`.**\n\nFrom `(1−x)·y = 1` and `x·(y−1)² = 1`.  Over any commutative ring, and with **no\nnon-vanishing hypothesis**: the identity\n\n    `x³ − (1−x)² = (1−x)²·(x(y−1)² − 1) − x·(x + (1−x)(y−1))·((1−x)y − 1)`\n\ndoes the elimination directly.  The mechanism is `(1−x)(y−1) = x`, which is `h1`\nrearranged. ","signatureChunk":0}]}